WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.199
Researchers map PFAS across 300 finger-lakes water bodies and found most concentrations remain low despite widespread presence. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 215. Cornell undergraduates gathered more than 500 samples, according to reporting from Fizz.org. Collection covered every one of the 11 finger-lakes, plus tributaries, ponds, and even puddles that persistently pool after rain. The team screened each sample for 24 common PFAS compounds.

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:35.359
systems. Alex Vendon-Henday built the map infrastructure that displays both hot spots

00:00:35.359 --> 00:00:40.959
and overall regional patterns. Professor Damian Hellblings said local residents contacted

00:00:40.959 --> 00:00:47.019
him after the EPA announced drinking water regulations in 2023, yet no prior local data

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:52.279
existed to answer their questions. Elevated readings clustered near airports and former

00:00:52.279 --> 00:00:58.499
fire training stations where deicing fluids and foams are known sources of PFAS. Gregory

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:03.999
Every pep in highlighted source control opportunities, Madeleine Adams is examining additional patterns

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:08.879
from repeated sampling, and the student team plans to use the spatial patterns to flag

00:01:08.879 --> 00:01:11.279
priority zones for expanded state monitoring.

00:01:12.528 --> 00:01:17.248
Undergraduates filled a local data gap at a scale that produced the first broad spatial picture

00:01:17.248 --> 00:01:19.328
of these persistent compounds in the region.

00:01:20.088 --> 00:01:22.848
Isolated hot spots exceed state guidance values.

00:01:23.348 --> 00:01:25.408
Those sites are not drinking water sources.

00:01:25.408 --> 00:01:30.628
They sit somewhat isolated from connected waterways, which limits their immediate downstream

00:01:30.628 --> 00:01:31.268
influence.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:36.428
The data set now serves as a baseline for tracking changes as new industries arrive.

00:01:37.088 --> 00:01:41.568
Whether similar student-led sampling campaigns could generate comparable baselines and other

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:45.788
New York watersheds before additional development occurs remains an open question.

00:01:46.824 --> 00:01:52.004
Most people assume a pollutant in a lake either thins into harmlessness or falls apart by itself.

00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:57.964
P-fast do neither. They resist breakdown, build up over time, and move wherever the water

00:01:57.964 --> 00:02:03.664
goes. Surface water volume was the main control on concentration in this survey, spreading

00:02:03.664 --> 00:02:09.584
the same total load across larger areas. Persistence is why a new local source can leave a measurable

00:02:09.584 --> 00:02:15.064
hotspot that lingers instead of flushing through. Runoff at a single site can stay detectable

00:02:15.064 --> 00:02:20.524
rather than vanishing downstream. Check water quality reports for your own region and see whether

00:02:20.524 --> 00:02:24.964
those programs already test for these compounds. Reports that skip them may

00:02:24.964 --> 00:02:29.264
understate the picture. Repeated sampling at the same sites after any new

00:02:29.264 --> 00:02:33.544
industrial activity begins would let later readings be compared against what is

00:02:33.544 --> 00:02:37.764
already in hand. Students on the project said the fieldwork shifted their own

00:02:37.764 --> 00:02:42.104
career interest toward community engaged environmental monitoring. The team

00:02:42.104 --> 00:02:46.464
intends to apply the same spatial approach to identify high priority areas in

00:02:46.464 --> 00:02:50.224
and other parts of New York, where monitoring programs are still developing.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:56.191
OBS Golden Retrievers in the Morris Animal Foundation Golden Retriever Lifetime Study

00:02:56.191 --> 00:03:01.391
faced more than twice the risk of endocrine disease, osteoarthritis, and cruciate ligament

00:03:01.391 --> 00:03:03.751
injury compared with dogs at a healthy weight.

00:03:04.271 --> 00:03:09.191
Data-compared dogs across healthy, overweight, and obese body-conditioned scores for disease

00:03:09.191 --> 00:03:14.491
risk, physical activity levels, and cognitive function, according to Fizz.org.

00:03:14.491 --> 00:03:20.651
Obese dogs also recorded lower physical activity and greater signs of cognitive decline with age.

00:03:21.251 --> 00:03:28.211
Cognitive screening asked owners about disorientation in familiar places, failure to recognize family members or other pets,

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:32.191
nighttime restlessness or pacing, and loss of house training.

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:37.511
Gradual diet and activity adjustments remain the primary route to maintaining healthy weight,

00:03:37.911 --> 00:03:42.291
with daily walks, play, or swimming tailored to the dog's age and fitness level.

00:03:42.291 --> 00:03:47.591
The aim is preserving mobility and quality of life rather than simply reducing scale weight.

00:03:48.348 --> 00:03:53.148
A group of previously unknown viruses shares architectural features once thought unique

00:03:53.148 --> 00:03:56.568
to either viruses or protein-based cellular compartments.

00:03:57.168 --> 00:04:01.908
University of Miami researchers identified them through genomic and structural analyses,

00:04:02.388 --> 00:04:04.328
a finding carried by Fizz.org.

00:04:04.988 --> 00:04:09.228
Shared architectural elements had been treated as a clean divide between the two categories.

00:04:09.228 --> 00:04:15.328
The virus is supply an evolutionary intermediate that may clarify how viruses and cells diverged

00:04:15.328 --> 00:04:15.948
over time.

00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:21.588
Direct implications reach biotechnology that relies on viral vectors and models of early

00:04:21.588 --> 00:04:22.388
life chemistry.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.440
Expanded excavations at White Sands National Park refine the age of the oldest known human

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.900
footprints in North America.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.260
The digs reconstructed landscape and environmental conditions present when the tracks were made,

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.920
in research described by Fizz.org.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.880
Researchers gained clearer evidence of abrupt shifts in local conditions during the period

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:43.800
of human presence.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.940
Additional excavation volume allowed tighter chronological control.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:52.860
That extra volume also produced a more complete picture of the setting in which the footprints

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:53.780
were preserved.

00:04:54.719 --> 00:05:01.039
Reef-building coral species now face elevated extinction risk in 44% of cases in a University of

00:05:01.039 --> 00:05:04.579
Portsmouth-led International Assessment reported by Fizz.org.

00:05:04.579 --> 00:05:09.899
work. The true figure is likely higher once data gaps are filled. The assessment updates

00:05:09.899 --> 00:05:15.339
conservation priorities for marine ecosystems worldwide. Field observations and modeling

00:05:15.339 --> 00:05:21.219
from the most recent records produce the revised threat classification. Biodiversity persists

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:26.979
in areas managed for agriculture, forestry, or other uses. Not only inside formal national

00:05:26.979 --> 00:05:33.479
parks and reserves, researchers argue in coverage from Fizz.org. The approach aims to inform upcoming

00:05:33.479 --> 00:05:38.759
coming United Nations biodiversity discussions in Armenia by recognizing working landscapes

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:40.599
that already support biodiversity.

00:05:40.999 --> 00:05:45.239
The framework expands options for maintaining species and habitats at scale.

00:05:45.959 --> 00:05:49.199
Ecological data from multiple regions underpins the analysis.

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:53.799
Effective conservation can occur in areas managed for other primary uses.

00:05:54.878 --> 00:05:59.778
New computational checks on electron density provide more reliable starting points for modeling

00:05:59.778 --> 00:06:02.178
molecules that contain several metal centers.

00:06:02.178 --> 00:06:07.718
measures. Such molecules appear in catalysts, battery materials, and metallo-enzymes, in

00:06:07.718 --> 00:06:12.598
a finding carried by Fizz.org. Better initial conditions reduce errors and predictions

00:06:12.598 --> 00:06:18.058
that guide laboratory synthesis. The method addresses a known source of uncertainty in simulations

00:06:18.058 --> 00:06:24.780
of complex, inorganic, and organometallic systems. Younger African-American adults express a stronger

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:29.480
preference for family responsibility in caring for older relatives than older cohorts did.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:34.780
University of Rhode Island researchers examined attitudes toward elder support across different

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.760
African-American age groups, in findings reported by Fizz.org.

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.120
The findings add detail to public health planning around aging populations.

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:48.580
Responses distinguish preferences by generational cohort within the same broad demographic.

00:06:49.507 --> 00:06:55.027
Before we go, upcoming United Nations biodiversity discussions in Armenia are set to take up how

00:06:55.027 --> 00:06:58.507
working landscapes outside parks can support species at scale.

